president biden is spending new year's  weekend at his home in wilmington  delaware and he's facing rising tensions  with russia to begin 2022. on friday he  spoke to reporters about his phone call  this week with russian president  vladimir putin schuyler henry is at the  white house with the latest schuyler  good morning  haley good morning to you and a happy  new year to you as well well it was a  relatively quiet week for president  biden however he did have that hour-long  phone call with russian president  vladimir putin it was a call requested  by the kremlin the two men discussed the  ongoing concerns at the russian  ukrainian border as well as other  security issues it was the second time  the two spoke in the last few weeks  white house officials also say president  biden will be speaking with ukrainian  president vladimir silinski at some  point tomorrow reaffirming the us's  support for ukraine's sovereignty  that meeting stems from growing fears of  a russian invasion into ukraine now  moscow stays around 100 000 troops along  ukraine's border but denies imminent  invasion in early december russia  removed around 10 000 troops from the  area however those with intelligence  suspect a possible invasion in the  coming weeks while russian officials  have downplayed that saying that is not  their intent now president biden was  asked about that yesterday when he and  the first lady were out to lunch he said  that he made it clear to putin that if  an invasion were to happen there would  be severe sanctions and an increased u.s  presence in europe with nato allies now  president biden also said that russia  has agreed to three conferences in  europe starting in geneva in nine days  president biden also adding that  progress would only continue if  president putin de-escalated the  situation on the ukrainian border  president biden and president putin  meeting again on january 10th to  continue those security talks elise a  lot to keep watching skyler henry at the  white house thanks
 

